    "Body":  "{\"id\":2,\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"result\":{\"tools\":[{\"description\":\"[AI -\u003e UE Plan Submit] Submit a PRV plan (Plan-Resolve-Verify Phase 1) and obtain a plan_id.\\n\\n=== WHEN TO USE ===\\nCall this tool ONCE before making ue_py calls that mutate editor state.\\nThe returned plan_id can be reused across multiple ue_py invocations (for the same asset)\\nuntil its TTL expires. This avoids re-sending the full YAML plan every time.\\n\\nUsage flow:\\n  1. ue_plan_submit { plan: \u003cYAML\u003e, reasoning: \u003cwhy\u003e }  → returns { plan_id, expires_at_seconds }\\n  2. ue_py          { code: \u003ccode\u003e, plan_id: \u003cid\u003e }      → executes with plan already bound\\n\\n=== PLAN YAML SCHEMA ===\\nRequired fields:\\n  intent          : one-line description of the goal (string)\\n  asset_path      : /\u003cProjectName\u003e/Asset/...  (string; /Game/ is rejected)\\n  mutations OR scene_ops (at least one non-empty)\\n    - mutations   : list of { property, value, gate? } — for CDO writes (asset properties)\\n    - scene_ops   : list of { op, klass?, label?, folder?, fields? } — for level-actor mutation\\n                    op ∈ {actor_spawn, actor_modify, actor_destroy, actor_set_folder}\\nOptional:\\n  apis_to_call    : list of API symbols (e.g. py:save_package, world.actor_spawn)\\n                    - apis_strict=false (default): optional; unknown entries → warning only\\n                    - apis_strict=true           : required and every entry must be in whitelist\\n  apis_strict     : bool (default false)\\n  pre_write_snapshot: bool (default true)\\n\\n=== EXAMPLE A — CDO mutations (asset edit) ===\\nArguments:\\n  reasoning: \\\"change weapon damage and mag size\\\"\\n  plan: |\\n    intent: \\\"Custom_AWM_Sniper: BaseImpactDamage=300, MaxBulletNumInOneClip=20\\\"\\n    asset_path: /TestNavmesh/Asset/Weapons/Custom_AWM_Sniper\\n    pre_write_snapshot: true\\n    apis_to_call:\\n      - py:load_object\\n      - py:get_cdo\\n      - py:get_uproperty\\n      - py:has_metadata\\n      - py:save_package\\n    mutations:\\n      - property: BaseImpactDamage\\n        value: \\\"300\\\"\\n        gate: bIsAttributeOverride\\n      - property: MaxBulletNumInOneClip\\n        value: \\\"20\\\"\\n        gate: bIsAttributeOverride\\n\\n=== EXAMPLE B — scene_ops (level building) ===\\nArguments:\\n  reasoning: \\\"build phase1 air walls + nav volume\\\"\\n  plan: |\\n    intent: \\\"Phase1 air walls + NavMesh\\\"\\n    asset_path: /TestMap/UGCmap\\n    apis_strict: false\\n    apis_to_call:\\n      - helpers.scene_apply\\n      - helpers.actor_spawn_volume\\n      - editor_command_save_current_level\\n    scene_ops:\\n      - op: actor_spawn\\n        klass: StaticMeshActor\\n        label: AirWall_North\\n        folder: Map/AirWalls\\n      - op: actor_modify\\n        label: AirWall_North\\n        fields: \\\"bHidden=true; SetCastShadow(false)\\\"\\n      - op: actor_destroy\\n        label: BP_STPlayerStart_2\\n      - op: actor_set_folder\\n        label: AirWall_North\\n        folder: Map/AirWalls\\n\\nOn success: { success:true, plan_id:\\\"plan_...\\\", expires_at_seconds:..., warnings:[] }\\nOn failure: { success:false, error:{ code, message, missing_fields:[...] } }\\n\\n=== RULES ===\\n1. One plan per asset. For multi-asset workflows, submit multiple plans.\\n2. Plan must be validated: missing required fields → server returns PRV_PLAN_INVALID.\\n3. plan_id has TTL (default 15 min). Re-submit if expired.\\n4. Server rejects asset_path starting with /Game/ (UGC assets live under /\u003cProjectName\u003e/Asset/ or /\u003cProjectName\u003e/\u003cMapName\u003e).\\n5. mutations and scene_ops can coexist; only constraint is at least one non-empty.\\n\",\"fastmcp\":{\"version\":\"3.1.1\"},\"inputSchema\":{\"properties\":{\"plan\":{\"description\":\"REQUIRED. PRV plan as YAML (preferred) or JSON. Must contain intent, asset_path, mutations, apis_to_call.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"reasoning\":{\"description\":\"Optional. Why you are submitting this plan (trace/audit).\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"ttl_seconds\":{\"description\":\"Optional. Custom TTL in seconds. Default 900 (15 min). Clamped to [30, 3600].\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"plan\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"name\":\"ue_plan_submit\"},{\"description\":\"[AI -\u003e UE Read] Query editor information from UGCEditor.\\n\\nSupported query prefixes (use as `queries: [\\\"\u003cprefix\u003e:\u003cparam\u003e\\\", ...]`):\\n  - ctx:[sub]               Current editor context (project/map/selected actors/opened assets).\\n                            Empty sub returns full context. Examples: \\\"ctx:\\\", \\\"ctx:selected\\\".\\n  - qt:[name]               List all structured query_type names; or get usage of one.\\n                            Examples: \\\"qt:\\\" (index), \\\"qt:bp\\\", \\\"qt:struct\\\".\\n  - py:\u003ckeyword\u003e            Python API doc lookup. Supports `py:workflow \u003cname\u003e` /\\n                            `py:\u003cmethod\u003e` / `py:\u003ckeyword\u003e` for fuzzy match.\\n  - schema:\u003cTypeName\u003e       Reflection schema (UClass/UStruct fields). Use exact name with\\n                            U/A/F prefix; for BP assets use full path ending with _C.\\n  - subclasses:\u003cBaseClass\u003e  Discover available subclasses of a base UClass.\\n  - bt:[nodes [filter]]     Behavior tree nodes enumeration / search by keyword.\\n  - enum:\u003cEnumName\u003e         Enum values.\\n\\nStructured entry (alternative to prefixes, for richer params):\\n  Pass `query_type=\u003cName\u003e` plus extra fields. Discoverable via `qt:` (e.g. bp / struct /\\n  classmember / objed / skilldoc / fusion / hierarchy / context / bt / enum).\\n\\nBatch: up to 10 queries in one call. Returns {mode:\u0027batch\u0027, received, executed,\\n       results:[{index, query, success, output}, ...]}.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  ue_read { queries: [\\\"ctx:\\\"] }\\n  ue_read { queries: [\\\"ctx:\\\", \\\"py:workflow skill\\\", \\\"schema:FPESkillTaskMoveTo\\\"] }\\n  ue_read { queries: [\\\"subclasses:UPESkillTask\\\", \\\"bt:nodes attack\\\"] }\\n  ue_read { query_type: \\\"bp\\\", asset_path: \\\"/Game/BP_MyActor\\\" }\\n\",\"fastmcp\":{\"version\":\"3.1.1\"},\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"properties\":{\"level\":{\"default\":1,\"description\":\"Detail level (0-3), default 1.\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"queries\":{\"description\":\"Query strings array (1-10 items). Single query: [\\\"ctx:\\\"], batch: [\\\"ctx:\\\", \\\"py:workflow skill\\\", \\\"schema:PESkillTask\\\"]. Returns {mode:\u0027batch\u0027, results:[{index,query,success,output},...]}.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":10,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"query_type\":{\"description\":\"Optional. Structured query type name. Use qt:\u003cname\u003e in queries to get usage details first.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"reasoning\":{\"description\":\"Recommended. Short explanation of what you want to query and why. Strongly encouraged for traceability.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"queries\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"name\":\"ue_read\"},{\"description\":\"[AI -\u003e UE Python] Execute Python code in UGCEditor.\\nImport: \u0027import unreal_engine as ue\u0027 (NOT \u0027import unreal\u0027). Classes: \u0027from unreal_engine.classes import ClassName\u0027.\\n\\n=== PRV (Plan-Resolve-Verify) ===\\nAny code that MUTATES state (setattr, save_package, actor_spawn, bt_add_node, etc.) requires a plan:\\n  1. RESOLVE: ue_read queries=[\\\"py:workflow \u003cdomain\u003e\\\", \\\"py:\u003capi\u003e\\\"] to learn APIs\\n  2. PLAN:   ue_plan_submit {plan:\u003cYAML\u003e} → plan_id   OR   ue_py {code, plan:\u003cYAML\u003e}\\n  3. EXECUTE: ue_py {code, plan_id} — server auto-verifies\\nPure-query code (no writes) needs no plan. skip_prv=true bypasses (only on user request).\\nPlan YAML: intent, asset_path, apis_to_call, mutations[{property,value}]. Details → ue_read queries=[\\\"py:workflow blueprint\\\"].\\n\\n=== DISCOVERY ===\\nALWAYS query before coding — NEVER guess API signatures or property names:\\n  • ue_read queries=[\\\"py:workflow \u003cname\u003e\\\"] — full workflow examples (scene/blueprint/skill/bt/property/viewport/objed/asset_browser/datatable/lua)\\n  • ue_read queries=[\\\"py:\u003cmethod\u003e\\\"]        — API signature \u0026 usage\\n  • ue_read queries=[\\\"py:index\\\"]           — full API category listing\\n  • ue_read queries=[\\\"schema:\u003cClassName\u003e\\\"] — property list with types/enums/tooltips\\n  • ue_read queries=[\\\"subclasses:\u003cBase\u003e\\\"]  — derived class list\\n  • ue_read queries=[\\\"enum:\u003cEnumName\u003e\\\"]    — valid enum values\\nProperty access: PascalCase (obj.PropertyName) for UE reflection; snake_case (obj.get_actor_location()) for PyCFunction.\\n\\n=== RULES ===\\n1. Provide \u0027instruction\u0027 (recommended) and \u0027transaction_name\u0027 for undoable mutations.\\n2. Use ue.log() for output; assign __askq_result for structured return values.\\n3. CDO writes need EditCondition TWO-PHASE: open gates → write values → save → verify. See py:workflow property.\\n\\n=== PITFALLS ===\\n- FRotator(roll, pitch, yaw) NOT (pitch,yaw,roll); FVector(x,y,z).\\n- actor_spawn/all_actors: WORLD methods — world = ue.get_editor_world(); world.actor_spawn(...).\\n- No \u0027ActorLocation\u0027 UProp. Use RootComponent.RelativeLocation or set_actor_location(FVector(...)).\\n- save_package: OBJECT method — bp.save_package(), NOT ue.save_package(bp).\\n- Asset paths: /\u003cProjectName\u003e/Asset/..., NOT /Game/. Use ue.get_project_root().\\n- Instanced sub-objects: ue.new_object(Class, owning_obj) — Outer MUST be property holder.\\n- Blueprint ↔ Lua: every BP under Asset/ has an associated .lua in Script/. Use bp_lua_get_path (read-only) or bp_lua_find_or_create (creates if missing). See py:workflow lua.\\n\",\"fastmcp\":{\"version\":\"3.1.1\"},\"inputSchema\":{\"properties\":{\"code\":{\"description\":\"REQUIRED. Python code to execute. Must use \u0027import unreal_engine as ue\u0027. Supports multi-line.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"instruction\":{\"description\":\"Recommended. Short explanation of your plan and what this Python code will do. Optional but strongly encouraged for traceability.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"plan\":{\"description\":\"REQUIRED for any code that writes/mutates editor state (assignment, save_package, actor_spawn, bt_add_node, etc.). YAML plan declaring intent/asset_path/mutations/apis_to_call. Omitting this for mutation code triggers warnings (Observe mode) or rejection (Enforce mode). Only pure-query code (no writes) may omit plan. See PRV WORKFLOW section above. Alternative: use plan_id from ue_plan_submit instead.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"plan_id\":{\"description\":\"Optional. A plan_id previously returned by ue_plan_submit. When present, the server resolves the bound plan from store and uses it for PRV validation (takes precedence over inline `plan`). Preferred for multi-call workflows on the same asset.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"skip_prv\":{\"description\":\"Optional. Set to true to explicitly bypass PRV plan validation. The request will still run but the response will contain warnings. Use only when user explicitly asks for quick mode.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"transaction_name\":{\"description\":\"Optional. Transaction name for undo support. If provided, code will be wrapped in begin/end_transaction.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"code\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"name\":\"ue_py\"}]}}"
